That's the auth instructions, but auth isn't your problem yet. The A5 couldn't resolve `gitcode.com` at all, which is DNS, not credentials. You'd need to fix connectivity first, then the token would matter.

Set the git identity, which is harmless either way:

```bash
git config --global user.name yaolu0211
git config --global user.email apfhxc7pUWUZ-Bq1.yaolu0211@noreply.gitcode.com
```

Then test whether the box can reach the internet at all:

```bash
env | grep -i proxy
curl -I https://gitcode.com --max-time 10
```

If that fails, the proxy route:

```bash
export https_proxy=http://y84451117:PASSWORD@Hkgpqwg00206.huawei.com:8080
export http_proxy=$https_proxy
curl -I https://gitcode.com --max-time 10
```

If curl then succeeds, clone and it will prompt for your username and token.

Simpler path, given fremont already clones from gitcode without any of this. Clone there and copy over:

```bash
